---
const facets = [
  {
    title: 'Rules as entities',
    body: 'Every rule is one DataJob under one shared mcmr/rulebook flow for the whole instance, so its page lists every codebase that runs it and what each one last got.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/concepts/rulebook/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Verdict timelines',
    body: 'Each rule and subject pair becomes one DataHub assertion. A later run lands on the same assertion, so history reads as a timeline instead of a pile of documents.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/what-gets-published/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Run instances',
    body: 'Each writeback mints one DataProcessInstance, stamped on every result it reports, so a reader pivots from a rule’s timeline to the run that wrote it and back.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/what-gets-published/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Cost provenance',
    body: 'A contextual verdict states its backend, model, and token counts. The rule job rolls that up per codebase, so a rulebook of hundreds sorts by what it costs for what it finds.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/cost-provenance/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Incidents for intermittent findings',
    body: 'A subject that flips failing, passing, failing again raises an incident titled by the rule and file, closed the moment it settles, so a table that will not stay fixed surfaces on its own.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/incidents-and-contracts/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Contracts',
    body: 'A data quality contract states the repository-wide promise every rule that judged a whole table makes, derived from the table’s own key rather than stacked as a second document.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/incidents-and-contracts/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Structured properties',
    body: 'Lane, rule family, codebase, findings, tokens spent, and flap score are typed DataHub properties, not a string in a table nobody can sort or filter.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/what-gets-published/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Agents as users',
    body: 'A human answers for the codebase, an agent operates the checks, and the model that judged the contextual lane is credited too, rather than everything sharing one account.',
    href: '/mcmr/docs/datahub/why-metadata/',
  },
];
---

<section id="datahub" class="bg-primary text-primary-content border-b-2 border-base-300">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase opacity-70">The metadata backbone</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl">A rulebook the next agent can read</h2>
      <p class="text-primary-content/85">
        MCMR keeps no cache of its own. When you ask it to, it writes what a run learned into
        DataHub, the catalog most data teams already run, so the conclusion lives beside the asset
        it is about instead of in a report only MCMR can open.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-px border-2 border-base-content bg-base-content sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {
        facets.map((facet) => (
          <a
            href={facet.href}
            class="group bg-base-100 text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 flex flex-col gap-2 p-6 transition-colors"
          >
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold" style="font-family: var(--font-brand)">
              {facet.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="text-base-content/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">{facet.body}</p>
            <span class="mt-auto pt-2 text-xs font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">
              Read more
            </span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <a href="/mcmr/docs/datahub/why-metadata/" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm mt-10">
      Why MCMR writes to DataHub at all
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
